skill:          gob (SKILL.md; LICENSE.md is the project's, beside it)
upstream:       https://github.com/juanibiapina/gob
path:           skills/gob/SKILL.md
tag:            v3.9.0
license:        MIT (LICENSE.md beside it)
vendored:       2026-10-19
deployed as:    ~/.claude/skills/gob (copy; config.linux.toml). Linux only, like gob itself:
                config.toml's ~/.claude/skills entry excludes this directory, so Windows,
                which has no gob build, never gets a skill that points at a missing binary.
note:           The tag is the gob pin's (config.linux.toml, github:juanibiapina/gob), so the
                skill describes the CLI that is installed; check_pins holds the two equal.
                scripts/bump-versions.sh re-vendors SKILL.md and LICENSE.md at the new tag
                when it bumps the pin, and updates tag and vendored here. Never hand-edit.
